  "body": "Part of #290 (design decisions D1-D10 in its research comment).\n\nDepends on: #531.\n\nThe electrode is the tool (an electrode solid in the tool library, with its length and pickup offset). Depth is measured from a stated datum: work top, cavity floor or electrode tip. The plunge is generated as CL moves; the existing 3-axis stock sim verifies it against the part (D7).\n\n**Done means:** a rectangular electrode burns a cavity to the stated depth, and a depth past the floor datum is refused. CL golden committed.",
